A||||5||Groot||Fiero 2.5L on LPG ( gas )
Z||000000||Groot||08-24-99||07:23 AM||||Hi, i have a 84 Fiero 2.5L running on LPG<br>instead of gasoline. Temperatures inside<br>the engine are much higher now. Do i have<br>to modify anything to make sure the Fiero<br>won't die on me too soon ?
Z||000001||DJRice||08-24-99||08:21 AM||||How much hotter is it exactly?  I dont know anything about the natural gas conversions for car engines, but if you are concerned you could put a lower temp thermostat in, and lock your fan on all the time.<p>Another thing you could do is find a later model Fiero with the Louvered Panels and swap them for the solid panels that came with the 84.  These were designed to pull heat out of the engine comparment.  Im talking about the panels that cover up your battery on one side and nothing on the other in the case of the 4 cyl.
Z||000002||Groot||08-24-99||08:42 AM||||Hi,<p>It's a good idea about those louvred panels.<br>I will look out for them.<p>My concern is not the temperature of the<br>coolant, but the internal temperature of<br>the valves etc. Some cars here in Europe<br>are modified with different heads to<br>be armed against the high temperatures.<p>A bill i found in my car proofed that the<br>valves have recently been changed.<p>Another problem is that the whole ECM<br>is confused now as LPG is totally different<br>of course. I might want to remove the<br>Check-Engine-Soon light.
Z||000003||theogre||08-24-99||09:35 AM||||My guess is that who ever did the LP conversion has screwed it up some how. Obviously an ECM designed for a gas engine it going to barf on LP. It would at the very least need reprogramming.<p>If your toasting valves I'd say the mix is off. Lean mix on a petrol motor is known for melting things, I'm guessing this is not much diferant. <p>The LP & LNG gas conversions I've seen done here, they are common only on Comercial Fleet vehicles, generally don't have these kind of problems. they are considered very reliable, but they are also designed specifically for the motors they are on.
Z||000004||lowCG||08-24-99||01:08 PM||||Had considered this on my car(4cyl)a couple years back.I don't know what different requuirements,as far as ignition timing goes,but an old pontiac sunfire distributor might simplify things a bit.<br>Is it an Impco valve?<br>Where are the tanks? Was going to make one that went in place of the gas tank,if I'd carried through with the plan.
Z||000005||Groot||08-26-99||01:42 AM||||Hi,<p>The LPG tank is a kind of sigar modelled<br>thing in the trunk of the car ....<br>48 liters. I have no place left for any<br>luggage at all !<br>( So the tank is between the engine and<br> the rear-lights )<p>It runs good on LPG and it seems rather<br>efficient with it. 6 miles on 1 ltr LPG
